Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 11/10/2023]
1. Resonance energies are a weighted average of Matos et al. 2011, Wrede et al. 2010, Afanasieva et al. 2017, Vouzoukas et al. 1994, and ENSDF.
2. Mirror assignments are based on Endt 1998 and Iliadis et al. 1999.
3. Gamma ray partial widths estimated from lifetimes of 32P mirror states (ENSDF, Endt 1998).
4. Proton partial widths estimated from spectroscopic factors measured in 31P(d,p)32P (Endt 1977, Eckle et al. 1989, Endt1990). Values are in overall agreement
   with shell-model results (also listed in Eckle et al. 1989).
5. Direct capture S factor estimated using spectroscopic factors measured in 31P(d,p)32P (Endt 1977, Eckle et al. 1989, Endt1990). Assumed factor of 1.7 uncertainty.
6. Er = 630 keV: we adopted the mean lifetime of the mirror state as listed in Endt 1998 [36(20) fs]. 


